Tirzah's iPhone (2): expansive, because I feel like there's a lot of people, again, when I was talking about, like, wide open spaces, I think people really like that. Peaceful is something else. That came to mind because of, like, Gen Z, they don't like chaos, they don't like to, you know, like, they want that calm atmosphere, so I think peaceful is good.

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:19.000
Alina Stevens: Thank you, bye-bye.

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): And.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): And those are some of the, I don't know, ones that I liked.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:40.000
Whitney Hodges: That's perfect. I think that's super helpful.

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:43.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Secluded is another one that I liked.

00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:45.000
Alina Stevens: I mean, is natural a word that you would use?

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:49.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): It can be. Yeah. Yeah, for sure. So.

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:29:47.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah, I think that would be a great one, because everything really is very natural and authentic, and, um, some places more than I want it to be. But, you know, it really is a space.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:12.000
Alina Stevens: for that person that… which kind of seems to be what Gen Z is right now, is, you know, they want everything to be real.

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Mm-hmm.

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Yeah.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.000
Alina Stevens: Damn.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:20.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Unhurried, unforgettable, um…

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:31.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I think private is a big deal, too. I think I'm curious about keywords in that area, because I know, like, in Charlotte, private…

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Okay.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Alina Stevens: Hmm?

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): was a big, like, keyword for us, and it was one of the things that drew a lot of people to us, because we were private and gated and surrounded by trees, and it wasn't like, you know, an uptown venue that everyone could just watch what was going on. So, um, yeah.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:49.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Okay.

00:30:49.000 --> 00:31:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, love it. Yeah, no, that's great. Just in kind of revisiting the spaces just a little bit, I'm seeing this really beautiful picture on the website of the Grand Pavilion with draping and chandeliers. Are those things always there or was that just…

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah. Yep.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Whitney Hodges: But they are.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Alina Stevens: Yes.

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:10.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Okay. Perfect. Yeah. Then I think we'll probably…

00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:08.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:19.000
Alina Stevens: In fact, I would tell you, we probably… I mean, Tirza can disagree with me if she wants, but we would probably charge to take them down, because they are not easy to put up and down.

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:21.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Oh yeah, we sure would.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, that totally makes sense. Yeah, but I think the fact that they're included is awesome. That's great. Okay, so other than what we just discussed about kind of the southern hospitality, the customer service.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:22.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:22.000
Alina Stevens: Okay, good.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:52.000
Whitney Hodges: The fact that they're getting the space just to themselves for the entire day, how kind of expansive and private it is. Any other top things that are coming to mind about why a couple should specifically book with the Dogwood?

00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:59.000
Whitney Hodges: We're good.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:00.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, yeah, cheers, that's…

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:04.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): My phone keeps freezing. I'm so sorry. I'm, like, touching it, trying to unmute myself.

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:11.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I would just say flexibility, because I think that is a big buzzword with people, you know, especially if we're gonna…

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:15.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Really lean into the DIY type of.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:20.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): client, I think flexibility has to be kind of high up there, too.

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:26.000
Whitney Hodges: Perfect. Great. Okay, that's helpful.

00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:41.000
Whitney Hodges: I know, again, that there haven't been, you know, a lot of tours or a lot of conversations yet. I think we've already kind of touched on, you know, potential objections, maybe, um, the, you know, the fact that the pavilions, you know, not climate controlled, other than the big fans.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:37.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, no.

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, I could imagine maybe, like, Rain Plan could, um, you know, come up on tours or, uh, discussions there. Any other potential objections you feel like we should be aware of and kind of, you know, trying to get ahead of in any of the…

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:59.000
Whitney Hodges: the ad copy or landing page copy.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Hmm…

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:17.000
Alina Stevens: Um, I mean, would you consider it an objection that we have horses on property, but, you know, they're not supposed to be in the barn, they're not supposed to be in the field with the horses, is that…

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:28.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): No. No, I mean, I think that's pretty logical. I don't know that someone would be like, well, I want to ride horses at my wedding. I don't think that that would be an objection, necessarily.

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:19.000
Alina Stevens: Something? Okay.

00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.000
Alina Stevens: Okay.

00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:28.000
Alina Stevens: Okay.

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:29.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Um…

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:36.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I think it's potential that an objection could be one of the things that we feel like is the best thing, is that it's so big.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmm.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:45.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): You know, because it is kind of far for Granny to go in her walker or whatever. Like, the…

00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.000
Alina Stevens: And…

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:51.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Restrooms could be potentially an objection, like, if you're, um…

00:33:51.000 --> 00:34:08.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I mean, it's just… you have to walk a bit. Like, the main restrooms for everyone are in the Grand Pavilion, so if you're having a wedding on the terrace, we're not going to be letting people come in the bridal suite to go to the bathroom. That's silly. So they would maybe have to walk a little ways to get to the restroom.

00:33:58.000 --> 00:33:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Right, right.

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:20.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I think that's kind of probably been one of the bigger ones that we've talked about as a team, is just, like, the restroom situation. They did renovate them, so they… they have enough in the pavilion, but…

00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:28.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): That could be one thing. I think the location, again, it's a pro and a con, right? So, it's pretty out there.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:22.000
Alina Stevens: Mm.

00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:29.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): And so, they don't necessarily have the convenience of, like.

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:36.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): What is it, Alina? 15 minutes to the closest town?

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:46.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah, well, I mean, it depends on what you're looking for. Like, to the grocery store is 10 minutes, to the closest town is probably 20-25.

00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:52.000
Alina Stevens: Um, so, like, your hotels and things that they would stay in is gonna be about 20-25 minutes.

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:56.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): So I would wonder how…

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:35:02.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): reliable Ubers and Lyfts would be. Probably not very reliable out there.

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:09.000
Alina Stevens: Right. So, I mean, we potentially can figure out a way to offer transportation.

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Yeah.

00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): that.

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:19.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Well, no, you just partner with a transportation company, you know, but there's probably not one in Greenville, so they would maybe have to get one from Atlanta. So, I'm just trying to think of all of the things that could be a possibility.

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:14.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:35:17.000 --> 00:35:22.000
Alina Stevens: Well, I bet there's something in Noonan, though. Let me look.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Well, you don't have to worry about it, but these are just kind of, like, we're just trying to think of, like, anything that someone could come and be like, oh my gosh.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:34.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): It's 30 minutes into the closest hotel, and, like, there's…

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:36.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah, but would that not be something that needs to be on the preferred vendor list?

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:39.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): It's one of my categories on there, yeah.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Alina Stevens: Okay, there's actually one in Luthersville, and Luthersville is…

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.000
Alina Stevens: 10 minutes up the road.

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): That's good. But again, so the… the objection helps us come up with a solution, right? So it's just, like, being able to handle the objections when they come up so that we know.

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:53.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, there's actually a lot of them.

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:55.000
Alina Stevens: Sure.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:03.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): There's no objection that we can't solve.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:04.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, and so really kind of what I'm getting at, and I know that we're talking about a lot of hypotheticals here, but this is kind of where having these, like, the… once you're fully onboarding, having the monthly strategy calls is really going to come into play, because you all are going to be able to fill us in on what the actual conversations are that are happening on tours. Like, what are the things that are…

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
Alina Stevens: Right.

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:40.000
Whitney Hodges: coming up, right? And then, so as you're letting us know those things, we can then make sure that we're weaving back into the ad copy, to the landing page copy, almost getting in front of those things from the very beginning, right? So maybe in the ad copy from the get-go, we need to say something about how.

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.000
Alina Stevens: Okay.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:40.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Awesome.

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:55.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, there are, uh, accommodations only 25 minutes from the venue, something along those lines, you know, overnight accommodations for the bride and groom, accommodations for your other out-of-town guests, just 25 minutes, something like that. So, um, not necessarily saying we need to do that from.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:52.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): What?

00:36:55.000 --> 00:37:02.000
Whitney Hodges: the start, but that's kind of how the process works ongoing, if that makes sense.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:08.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm. Yeah, as we get feedback, yes, obviously we will address it.

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Right, right, and…

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:16.000
Alina Stevens: But I don't want to throw it out there from the get-go. I don't want to start out going, hey, you know, yeah.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:22.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): No, no, so her point is that she takes the objection, and she turns the frown upside down, right? And so she just, like…

00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:23.000
Alina Stevens: Absolutely.

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:25.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): tries to get ahead of it. Yeah.

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Alina Stevens: I'm just saying, let's get the objection first, right? Mm-hmm.

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Exactly.

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Yeah. And so then the other thing to mention, which again is like more kind of future forward, would be about like customer research, analytics.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:29.000
Alina Stevens: Yes.

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:55.000
Whitney Hodges: market research, you know, things like that. One thing that we can do for you, if you're open to it, is within Leadlock, create a customer market research survey. And the purpose of this would be.

00:37:55.000 --> 00:38:15.000
Whitney Hodges: to send it out very shortly after a customer, a new client, a new couple books with you, maybe, like, within a week or so, to really get them to answer the why behind why they booked with you. And it would include, like, a combination of, you know, more kind of multiple choice questions, but also ways for them to.

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:06.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:31.000
Whitney Hodges: put it in their own words, right? And so then that helps us to start to be able to find, um, you know, the question that I asked earlier, how would an ideal couple describe what they're looking for? Well, we're going to be able to get it straight from the horse's mouth, right? Because they will then be answering.

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:30.000
Alina Stevens: Sure.

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:33.000
Whitney Hodges: the question.

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:36.000
Alina Stevens: Why would you not also do that to the clients that don't book?

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:40.000
Alina Stevens: So that we, therefore, by default, get the objections as well.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:57.000
Whitney Hodges: You can. You can try. I think that that probably is part of, like, the post-tour survey, I want to say, that Tirzah has maybe implemented for you guys. It's just you're a lot more likely to get a response from the couples that have actually booked.

00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:14.000
Whitney Hodges: than from the couples that haven't booked, if that makes sense. Like a lot of times, you know, after a tour, if somebody chooses to go a different way, or you might not even get a straight answer from them that they have booked a different venue, much less why they have booked.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah.

00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:04.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:21.000
Whitney Hodges: the other venue. So this is more about focusing in on exactly who your ideal client is, so that you can.

00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:27.000
Whitney Hodges: speak directly to more of them, right? Attract and pull more of those ideal clients in.

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:29.000
Alina Stevens: Okay.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): A lot of them, Alina, don't…

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:42.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): they just want you to go away at that point, and so I've tried this, actually, before a lot, and so we've been doing it even with a girl that had the tour and canceled.

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:38.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah, you know.

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:56.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Um, and some of the people, they had already just booked their venue, and so we would even ask them, like, where did you go? And then they just ghost us and then put us on D&D. So they just don't want to be bothered.

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:45.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:58.000
Alina Stevens: Yeah.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:40:04.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): So, even if you had that survey, a lot of them aren't going to fill it out, but we are physically asking them.

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:15.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): where they chose, and so sometimes they'll tell you. And when they come for a tour, it's part of our pre-tour survey, we ask them other venues that they visited, too. So, we're trying to get.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:15.000
Alina Stevens: Absolutely.

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:21.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): trying to figure out some of that stuff, but yeah. I mean, what Whitney is basically getting at is it's like…

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:32.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): it's evolving. This is never gonna be a static thing, like, as you grow and figure out, you know, our ideal client may change someday, you know?

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:37.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): But it's we just got to get more data in there. We just don't have it.

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:43.000
Alina Stevens: Mm-hmm. Seriously, I don't know if you did for Whitney, but you've gotten a little g.

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:45.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Hello, hello, there.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:45.000
Alina Stevens: Is she still clear for you, Whitney?

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, yeah, she's okay for me.

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:54.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, okay, maybe it's me. No, no, I heard everything, it was just a little…

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Sorry.

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:52.000
Whitney Hodges: And the.

00:40:54.000 --> 00:41:01.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): My… I'm cleaning my house because my cleaners changed their cleaning time, and I'm, like, prepping for my cleaners.

00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:56.000
Alina Stevens: Garbly. Okay.

00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:03.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, no!

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:07.000
Alina Stevens: You're one of those people that cleans before your cleaning people come?

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Uh, yes!

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:19.000
Whitney Hodges: I do, too. I mean, I… if I don't pick up, like, it'll be a disaster. Yeah, my husband gives me the hardest time about it. He's like, we're paying for somebody to clean the house, why are you cleaning it? I'm like.

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:12.000
Alina Stevens: I did not do that.

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:22.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I'm straightening! I'm straightening! It's fine.

00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes, exactly. Yeah.

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:28.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Alright, so does that help Whitney? I know that we're kind of all over the place.

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:25.000
Alina Stevens: Oh, funny.

00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:44.000
Whitney Hodges: No, you guys are fine. I think before I let you go, the one final question that I have, or kind of talking point I have for us, is the Dogwood Reserve versus, um, the competitors. And you gave us a very extensive list of competitors of other venues that you feel like, um, you know, people are checking out along with.

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, you guys. And, um, my question would be, you know, what is, what's your differentiator or differentiators? If somebody was choosing between the Dogwood, um, and one of those other venues, what do you think would tip the scale in your favor?

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:09.000
Alina Stevens: Oh goodness, I would have to go through and analyze each one, because obviously they're all similar to us, or different from us, for different reasons.

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep.

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:11.000
Alina Stevens: So…

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:26.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I… I say their biggest differentiator are the… I don't know any other ones that are over 200 acres, that it's, like, wide open spaces. Like, I think the… the seclusion, the natural beauty, just the, um…

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:13.000
Alina Stevens: Oh…

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:31.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): The flexibility and the open spaces, I think, is going to be the bigger thing.

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, awesome.

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:33.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): For them.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:34.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah. Okay.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Love it. Okay. Well, that totally makes sense.

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:36.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I'm not.

00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:52.000
